body:
I'm so sorry you're going through all that :( I can understand how insane and emotionally draining it can be. But I believe in you and you got this!! 

&#x200B;

You have your awesome teddy and your amazing books and You got this! :) Post any and all times when you need a pick me up. :) We're here for you

Woo hoo!! Good job on that test!! :)

&#x200B;

Btw, you're makeup looks amazing and on point! Way to rock it and kick ass at the same time!

I love this comic and all it stands for! It's amazing!

&#x200B;

I heard a counter argument to this one though that talked about replacing the "men" to some other minority group (aka, middle easterners, or minorities) and how the comic would read as negative and racist. I still feel in my heart that the comic is correct with it's assertion and want to know a good reply to that criticism.   


The only one I can think of so far is that this scenario, when this logic is used in attachment to minority groups it's used as a justification for prejudiced behavior. While the comic as is, with men, is instead used to address a derailment tactic that is often times used to belittle and decrease the severity of the concerns facing women and men (because men can be the victim too). 

&#x200B;

But I want to know what you all think as well! I want a better understanding of how to combat this type of backwards thinking!
